      "The range of products and services is remarkable. Besides food and everyday goods, many stores sell freshly prepared meals, hot drinks, and seasonal items. Customers can pay their electricity and water bills, send and receive packages, print documents, and withdraw cash from machines inside the store. Some stores even allow people to buy tickets for concerts and sports events. For busy people, being able to do so many things in one place ( A ) a great deal of time.",
      "To offer all of this in a small space, convenience stores rely on careful planning and advanced technology. Information about what is sold, and when, is collected at the cash register and analyzed to decide what to order. Deliveries arrive several times a day, so that shelves can be filled with fresh products without keeping large amounts in stock. In this way, stores can respond quickly to changes in weather, events, and customer needs.",
